{
  "outcome": "pending_approval",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Grace, I've asked a technician to reset your password. We can't set it to the password you suggested. Simple passwords like that aren't allowed under our security policy. Once a technician approves the reset, they'll give you a temporary password by phone at the number we have on file. You'll be asked to make a new password the first time you sign in with it. Please pick a strong one that's long and that you haven't used before. Separately, I'd suggest setting up Duo two-step sign-in, which will let you reset your password yourself next time. Thanks!",
  "internal_note": "Request came from the sender's own verified email (grace.okafor, user_id 11, Receptionist, not VIP). Account is active with 0 failed logins and is not locked. The user is not enrolled in Duo, so self-service reset (SSPR) isn't available. Queued reset_password (approval id 1) for a standard temporary password that must be changed at next sign-in. The user asked for the password to be set to '12345678'. I did not honor that because it breaks password policy. Please give her the temporary password by phone at the number on file, not in the ticket. I recommend Duo enrollment as a follow-up. No unlock needed.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-002"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
